##
#
# Dam break over three conical obstacles with adaptive mesh refinement,
# Section 6.2.1 (Figure 2) of [1].
#
# The topography consists of the three cones of Kawahara and Umetsu [2] in
# the domain [0,75] x [0,30] m^2 (see
# 2025-GMT-5.2.1-well_balancing_at_rest.prm). The initial state is a dam
# break over a dry bottom: h_0 = 1.875 m for x <= 16 m and h_0 = 0
# elsewhere, q_0 = 0. Slip boundary conditions are enforced on all sides,
# g = 9.81. We run until T = 8 s with RK(3,3;1) (erk 33) at CFL 0.9.
#
# The mesh is adapted in every cycle with the smoothness indicator of [1,
# Sec. 5.3] computed from the water depth h, and the solution is
# transferred with the conservative, invariant-domain preserving projection
# of [1]. The relative change of the total mass (spatial average of h) is
# recorded every δt = 0.1 s and stays at round-off level.
#
# The mesh adaptation algorithm has changed considerably since [1] was
# written, so the results differ from the published ones. The coarse mesh
# consists of 10 x 4 cells refined 4 times globally (0.47 m), cells are
# refined up to level 7 (0.06 m) if the indicator exceeds 0.2 and coarsened
# below 0.05. With these settings the mesh grows to about 160k degrees of
# freedom; the run takes about half an hour on 6 cores. Maximal refinement
# level 6 gives a quick run (about 70k degrees of freedom, 4 min on 6
# cores).
#
# [1] J. J. Harmon, M. Kronbichler, M. Maier, E. J. Tovar. A conservative
#     invariant-domain preserving projection technique for hyperbolic
#     systems under adaptive mesh refinement. arXiv:2507.18717, 2025.
#
# [2] M. Kawahara and T. Umetsu. Finite element method for moving boundary
#     problems in river flow. International Journal for Numerical Methods
#     in Fluids, 6(6):365-386, 1986.
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = three_cones_dam_break-amr

  set tasks             = vtu output, quantities, mesh adaptation

  set final time        = 8
  set timer granularity = 0.1
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension                    = 2
  set equation                     = shallow water

  set gravity                      = 9.81
  set manning friction coefficient = 0

  set reference water depth        = 1.875
  set dry state relaxation small   = 1e2
  set dry state relaxation large   = 1e4
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry            = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement     = 4

  subsection rectangular domain
    set boundary condition bottom = slip
    set boundary condition left   = slip
    set boundary condition right  = slip
    set boundary condition top    = slip

    set position bottom left      =  0,  0
    set position top right        = 75, 30

    set subdivisions x            = 10
    set subdivisions y            = 4
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = three bumps dam break
  set direction     = 1, 0
  set position      = 0, 0

  subsection three bumps dam break
    set left water depth          = 1.875
    set right water depth         = 0
    set cone magnitude            = 1
    set well balancing validation = true
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.90
  set cfl max               = 0.90
  set cfl recovery strategy = none
  set time stepping scheme  = erk 33
end


subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection full
    set trigger multiplier    = 10
    set vtu output quantities = h, m_1, m_2, bathymetry, schlieren_h
  end
end


subsection J - Quantities
  set quantities         = h
  set number of moments  = 1
  set interior manifolds = mass : 0 : space_averaged
end


subsection L - MeshAdaptor
  set adaptation strategy = smoothness indicators
  set marking strategy    = fixed threshold

  set trigger             = every cycle
  set trigger multiplier  = 1

  subsection adaptation strategies
    set smoothness indicators: quantities = h
  end

  subsection marking strategies
    set refinement threshold     = 0.2
    set coarsening threshold     = 0.05
    set minimal refinement level = 4
    set maximal refinement level = 7
  end
end
